# Build context for the Python images (api, bootstrap, ingestion, processor).
#
# The context is this whole directory, and without this file every one of
# those builds uploaded ~150 MB to the daemon -- 143 MB of it being
# frontend/node_modules, which no Python image copies. On Docker Desktop
# that transfer happens before any build output appears, so a build looks
# hung when it is only shipping files it will never use.
#
# Keep this in step with the COPY lines in */Dockerfile: shared/, ai/,
# backend/app/, video-ingestion/, event-processor/, database/, config/ and
# the requirements.txt files must all still reach the build.

.git
.gitignore

# The web image builds from ./frontend as its own context; no Python image
# copies it. node_modules alone is 143 MB.
frontend

# Python build and test artefacts. Copied into images otherwise, where they
# are dead weight at best and stale bytecode at worst.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# Not copied by any Dockerfile.
tests
docs
*.zip
*.pptx

# Local state and secrets. .env in particular must never be baked into a
# layer -- it would ship credentials inside the image.
.env
data/
